<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qasim Barid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1504">1504</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Qasim Barid I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qasim Barid was a Turkic noble who became chief minister of the declining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> in the 1490s and controlled its last sultans from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a>. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barid-shahi-dynasty">Barid Shahi dynasty</a>, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir">Amir</a> Barid continued to rule in the Bahmanis' name before his descendants took the royal title as sultans of Bidar.</p></div>
